Original commit body from 7b17b2ce4af606d7440b6d1fe4dd069fab1a5829:

A read-write property (a @property getter + a same-named @x.setter/@x.deleter)
dropped the read edge. Getter and setter share the qualified name C.x, and the
name-keyed symbol registries (symbol_by_name, the (path, qualified) index) are
last-write-wins, so they retain the SETTER — whose recorded decorator is the
dotted "x.setter" (not the bare "property"), failing the property-read
producer's gate in _resolve_property_getter. The getter was masked and c.x
emitted no edge (a documented D2 known gap).

Fix: _build_property_getter_index builds a dedicated (path, qualified_name) ->
getter map from the PRE-collapse per-file symbols, wired into both the
full-pipeline main loop and the single-file extract_nodes path and threaded
through _extract_edges. _resolve_property_getter consults it first, so a
read-write property's read now emits its receiver-type-hinted read edge
(resolvable via the inherited-calls linker) exactly as read-only properties do.
Covers getter+setter and getter+setter+deleter.

WI-sizut (G5). Flips the TestReadWritePropertyResolves gap tests to resolved.

